      "description": "Over 700 of this supersonic Air Launched Cruise Missile (ALCM) were produced, the type seeing USAF service from 1960 to 1978.\nThis example has previously been reported as being 62-0003, but not only was that a SM-68 Titan II, but it was launched from Vandenburg AFB in 1965. The nearest serial batch to this was 62-0030 to 62-0206, so it may be one of those.\nOn display on the inner pylon of a B-52 Stratofortress at the Castle Air Museum, Atwater, CA.\n\n4th March 2016",
